          "filePath": "src/storage.js",
          "lineNumber": 2,
          "explanation": "The `await` keyword was removed from `db.insert(row)`. Because `db.insert` returns a Promise, failing to await it means `store` will resolve with `{ saved: true }` before insertion finishes, and any insertion errors/rejections will be unhandled rather than rejecting the `store` promise.",
          "suggestedFix": "Restore `await` before `db.insert(row)` so that `store` waits for insertion to complete and properly propagates errors.",
          "evidence": "  db.insert(row);",
